1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,590
After a lifetime of struggle

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:04,530
and eventual success,

3
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:07,190
Charles Bukowski left two

4
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:09,050
words on his tombstone:

5
00:00:09,920 --> 00:00:11,650
'Don't try.'

6
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:14,850
He faced 30 years of rejection.

7
00:00:15,120 --> 00:00:16,430
His breakthrough at 50

8
00:00:16,440 --> 00:00:18,330
seemed like an underdog tale.

9
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:19,950
But success came

10
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:22,170
from accepting who he was,

11
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:24,290
not from wanting it more.

12
00:00:24,920 --> 00:00:27,110
This is 'The Backwards Law,'

13
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:28,490
from Alan Watts.

14
00:00:29,080 --> 00:00:31,450
The harder you chase good feelings,

15
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:33,610
the more they elude you.

16
00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:35,890
Straining for success

17
00:00:36,120 --> 00:00:38,050
makes you feel like a failure.

18
00:00:38,720 --> 00:00:41,150
Sometimes, the boldest moves

19
00:00:41,160 --> 00:00:42,790
only happen when we stop

20
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:44,730
obsessing over the outcome.

21
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:47,210
Accept discomfort,

22
00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:49,290
and it loses its power.

23
00:00:50,080 --> 00:00:50,870
What if you just

24
00:00:50,880 --> 00:00:52,440
let yourself feel it?
